WEBVTT

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.543
Did you know chess was invented in India?

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:06.944
About fifteen hundred years ago,
the game was called chaturanga.

00:00:07.209 --> 00:00:09.419
The name means four divisions of an army.

00:00:09.715 --> 00:00:12.965
There were foot soldiers,
horsemen, elephants, and chariots.

00:00:13.226 --> 00:00:15.096
The goal was to trap the enemy king.

00:00:15.387 --> 00:00:18.337
Soon, the game travelled to Persia,
and became shatranj.

00:00:18.957 --> 00:00:21.927
Persian players shouted shah mat
when they trapped the king.

00:00:22.203 --> 00:00:24.133
It means, roughly, the king is helpless.

00:00:24.564 --> 00:00:25.974
That is where we get checkmate.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:30.369
Arab traders carried the game west,
across North Africa to Spain.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.150
By about the year 1000,
chess was popular in Europe.

00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:38.071
The elephants became bishops,
and the chariots became rooks.

00:00:38.192 --> 00:00:41.982
At first, the queen was a weak
piece that moved one step at a time.

00:00:42.197 --> 00:00:47.107
Then, around 1475, she became the
most powerful piece on the board.

00:00:47.378 --> 00:00:49.668
The game became faster, and more exciting.

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:52.739
Today, over six hundred
million people play.

00:00:53.014 --> 00:00:56.344
A game from India,
that now belongs to the whole world.

